# All-lowercase type

No capital letters anywhere in the product UI. Brand constraint — do not override.

## Required

- Visible copy is **lowercase**: headings, nav, buttons, labels, placeholders, legal, empty states, toasts.
- CSS: inherit `text-transform: lowercase` from `body`. Never set `uppercase`, `capitalize`, or `full-width`.
- Do not use `font-variant: small-caps` (it reads as capitals).
- New hardcoded strings in Vue/JS must be written in lowercase (`gallery`, not `Gallery`).

```vue
<!-- ✅ -->
<button class="btn-primary">submit</button>
<h2>about me</h2>

<!-- ❌ -->
<button class="btn-primary">Submit</button>
<h2>About Me</h2>
```

```css
/* ✅ */
.home-about__title {
  letter-spacing: 0.22em;
}

/* ❌ */
.home-about__title {
  text-transform: uppercase;
  font-variant: small-caps;
}
```

## Exceptions

- Code, file names, env vars, URLs, and API keys are unchanged.
- User-typed form values may be stored as entered; **display** still lowercases via CSS.
